#### bodies
7:- **Record read for Node.** A new engine function `net::eol::verify_record_outside_session` refuses a record above `MAX_RECORD_BYTES`, the same cap as the gated fetch path. Then it parses the name, unmarshals the record, and verifies it with the core IPNS decoder. It is not a gated read: it adopts nothing, checks no floor, and does not compare the EOL with the time. It returns the sequence, the signed RFC3339 validity text, and the EOL in Unix millis. The WASM module exports it as `readIpnsRecord`, but only when the module is built with the `observer` feature of `crates/wasm`. By the owner decision of 2026-09-29 (ADR 0057 D1), the production module does not carry this export. The conformance build of the client Node suite enables `observer`. `apps/web` `build:wasm`, the Web Engine WASM job, the Web Bundle, staging deploy and the e2e builds enable no feature. `packages/client` exports `openIpnsRecordReader(glueUrl, wasmBinary)`, which loads the wasm-bindgen glue and returns a reader. If the module has no `readIpnsRecord`, the reader fails with an error that says that the module was built with no `observer` feature. TypeScript adds no codec. A record that another key signed, or a malformed record, throws the core check name.
8:- **Order of landing.** `tests/web-e2e/soak/recordReader.ts` has no caller yet. The soak spec that calls it lands with the soak batch. The comments in `crates/wasm/Cargo.toml`, `ci-web.yml` and `deploy-staging.yml` cite ADR 0057 D1. The ADR file lands with PR #2097, which merges directly after this PR.
9:- A replayed token gets 401 `Identity token already used`. This check runs before the identity check, so the refusal names the replay.
13:- `spend` runs the insert before the sweep, so a replayed token causes no sweep.
18:What this PR does not fix: the first acceptance item of #2012. The API cannot refuse "a token issued for another account", because the API has no fact that links a subject to an account before the first registration. `identity_subjects` has no `user_id` (ADR 0039 D1). `POST /auth/login` does not carry the identity token. Any secp256k1 key can create an account. On `main`, a new test showed that an account with a leaked token of another subject registers with 201. The spend in this PR does not change that first claim. To fix the bind, the login must present the identity token, and the API must bind the subject to the account at the first login. That change touches the engine API client, `packages/login`, both hosts and the contract suite. It also changes ADR 0039 D2, so it needs an ADR first. For this reason this PR is only part of #2012.
24:| A different account replays a token that a registration already spent | Refused with 401 |
25:| The same account replays a spent token | Refused with 401 |
29:The single-use rule stops only the replay of a spent token. It does not stop the first claim.
41:### Contract surface
43:The request and response shapes do not change. The 401 description of `POST /devices` and the `identityToken` field description change in `openapi.json`. The engine API client and `crates/contract` send the same fields. The contract test sends `not.a.token` and still gets 401.
45:The contract suite has no case for the replay refusal. The suite cannot get a real identity token: every mint needs a verified Google, email or wallet credential, and the email code goes to the mail log, which the suite cannot read. The API integration gate is the only proof of the replay refusal.
49:- [ ] Contract suite: no replay case. #2012 asks that the API gate and the contract suite block the merge, but the contract suite cannot mint a real identity token. Only the API integration gate blocks a regression of the replay refusal. The contract replay case is a duty of the account-bind slice, which gives the login the identity token.
50:- [x] `apps/api` unit suite: 483 passed. New tests: every token has its own token id, a token without `jti` or `exp` is refused, a token whose `jti` is not a UUID gets 401 before any spend, a token whose `exp` is `1e999`, `-1e999` or `1e300` is refused (and the same token gets 401 before any spend at registration), a replay is refused and writes nothing, a replay from another account is refused before the identity check, and the subject row holds no display key.
