Review two proposed ADRs of FSM1/cipher-box for issue #2108 (every file and folder record lapses 90 days after its last publish, because only the renewal set is renewed). Every `gh` call needs the prefix `env -u GITHUB_TOKEN`. Local main: `/Users/myankelev/Code/random/cipher-box` at `c0eb46e73`.

- PR #2109, ADR 0061 (the renewal walk), head `dbe473283`, branch `docs/adr-renew-every-name`. A first review found these problems; check that the revision closes each one, and look for new problems that the revision caused:
  1. same-device rollback: a drain publish can raise the floor during the `register` await, between the re-read and the signature;
  2. cross-device tie at one sequence: endpoints keep the later EOL (now fixed with a one-day-short renewal EOL);
  3. the bin: binned subtrees were not walked;
  4. a stopped name wave: old names lapse;
  5. a delete that races the walk re-registers a retired name;
  6. API throttles (`registry` 120/min, `recovery` 30/min per account, `apps/api/src/ops/throttling.ts`);
